course: dictionary
lesson: 4439
title: Handover: passing it on
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A handover is the act of passing something from one person or group to another. It can be a job, a power or a place. «In 1797 George Washington stepped down as US president after eight years, a peaceful handover of power.» The power moved from one leader to the next, and nobody had to fight for it.
explain: Handover can also mean a short meeting where one worker tells the next worker what they need to know. Nurses do this at the end of a shift, so the next nurse knows how each patient is doing. Here the handover is the talk, not the thing being passed.
explain: In a relay race, a handover is when a runner passes the baton to the next runner. Sports people often call this a changeover. Look for the phrase «a smooth handover»: it means the passing goes easily, with no dropped baton and no lost speed.
fact: A handover is the act of passing something from one person or group to another.
fact: «A smooth handover» means passing something on easily, with no problems.
fact: «Handover of power» means one leader or group gives control to another.
fact: A shift handover is a quick meeting where one worker tells the next what they need to know.
fact: In a relay race, the handover of the baton is also called the changeover.
exercise: «In 1797 George Washington stepped down as US president, a peaceful handover of power.» What is a handover of power? | A fight for control of the country | *Passing power from one leader to the next | A new kind of election for children | A long holiday from work
exercise: Nurses do a handover at the end of a shift. What is it? | *A meeting where one worker tells the next what they need to know | A party to celebrate the end of the day | A test that every nurse must pass | A list of things to buy
exercise: In a relay race, another word for handover is the changeover. What is a changeover in a race? | The starting gun | A runner who falls over | The finish line | *Passing the baton to the next runner
test:
«Their team made a smooth handover, and nobody dropped the baton.» What does smooth mean here? | Rough and bumpy | *Easy, with no problems | Slow and noisy | Very loud
Jess asks, «What is a handover?» Which answer is best? | Keeping a secret from everyone | *Passing something from one person or group to another | Running a race all by yourself | Forgetting a task you were given
exam:
Ruby reads «a handover of power» and asks what it means. Which answer is right? | Power is lost forever | *Control passes from one group to another | Power is stored in a box | A king is crowned
